1
00:00:01,041 --> 00:00:09,031
Welcome to Supply Flow. This video shows nurses everything they need, step by step, in a simple way.

2
00:00:09,482 --> 00:00:14,862
Open the system link. Write your name and your password, then tap Sign in.

3
00:00:15,314 --> 00:00:41,304
On the New request page, there are three choices at the top. One: Doctor request, for supplies used by one doctor. The doctor must approve it. Two: Clinic consumables, for supplies used by the whole clinic, and for sterilization. No doctor approval is needed. Three: Send to lab, for patient work that goes to the dental lab.

4
00:00:41,755 --> 00:00:48,215
Let's start with a Doctor request. Choose the doctor. The clinic and the branch are filled in for you.

5
00:00:48,666 --> 00:00:55,696
Choose the type. Monthly is your normal monthly order. Emergency is only for urgent needs.

6
00:00:56,146 --> 00:01:02,216
Now add the items. Tap the search box, write part of the name, and tap the item.

7
00:01:03,058 --> 00:01:06,398
Use plus and minus to set how many you need.

8
00:01:06,874 --> 00:01:15,344
Check the summary on the side, then tap Submit request. Your draft is saved by itself, so you never lose your work.

9
00:01:15,795 --> 00:01:28,755
Next, Clinic consumables. Use it for things the whole clinic uses, like gloves or cotton. Choose Clinic consumables, then choose your clinic, and add the items.

10
00:01:29,206 --> 00:01:35,636
Tap Submit request. This request goes straight to procurement. It does not wait for a doctor.

11
00:01:36,087 --> 00:01:50,537
Sterilization supplies are ordered the same way, as Clinic consumables. Open the clinic list. The Sterilization section is at the top. Choose the sterilization of your branch: Buraydah or Unayzah.

12
00:01:50,988 --> 00:01:57,488
A note shows exactly where the order will be delivered. Add the items and tap Submit request.

13
00:01:59,597 --> 00:02:14,377
Now open My requests. Here you can see the difference. The doctor request shows Doctor review: it waits for the doctor. The clinic and sterilization requests show New: they went straight to procurement.

14
00:02:14,827 --> 00:02:22,247
Tap Details to see everything about a request: each step and its time, the items, and the comments.

15
00:02:22,698 --> 00:02:32,008
The doctor gets an email automatically. Ask the doctor to open their page and approve. You can also write a comment here as a reminder.

16
00:02:32,460 --> 00:02:38,320
This is the doctor's page. The doctor sees the requests that are waiting for approval.

17
00:02:40,768 --> 00:02:47,748
The doctor opens the request. The doctor can change a quantity or add a note, and then taps Approve.

18
00:02:48,206 --> 00:02:56,796
After approval, procurement prepares the order and sends it to your branch. You get an alert, and the request shows Sent.

19
00:02:58,867 --> 00:03:08,657
When the box arrives, open My requests and tap Receive and sign. Check each quantity. If something is missing, change the number.

20
00:03:09,107 --> 00:03:16,647
Sign in the box with your finger, then tap Confirm receipt. A receipt with your signature is saved.

21
00:03:17,098 --> 00:03:30,488
Now, sending work to the lab. Choose Send to lab, choose the doctor, and write the patient file number. The scan date is today. Change it only if the scan was on another day.

22
00:03:30,939 --> 00:03:44,599
Add the work: choose the lab, the type of work, and write notes, like the tooth number and the shade. You can add a photo for each work. The date the lab must finish is calculated for you.

23
00:03:45,062 --> 00:03:49,362
Tap Send to lab. Now you can follow it on the Lab page.

24
00:03:49,821 --> 00:03:59,561
When the lab finishes, it sends the work back to the clinic. You will see the button Confirm receipt. Tap it when the work reaches your clinic.

25
00:04:00,011 --> 00:04:15,561
That's all. Doctor requests need the doctor's approval. Clinic and sterilization requests go straight to procurement. Lab work goes to the lab. If there is any problem, use the Report button on the card. Thank you!
